I have everything needed. Here is the full report.

# Identity fields exploration: `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, `checkDigit`

## Repository shape
- Build system: **Maven** (single `pom.xml`, no Gradle). Project `org.springframework.samples:spring-petclinic-rest:4.0.2` on Spring Boot 4.1.0.
- This is Spring PetClinic REST **converted to OfficeFloor function injection**. The `POST /api/owners` pipeline is wired in YAML, not Java controllers.
- `OwnerDto` is **not** checked into the tree — it is generated at build time by `openapi-generator-maven-plugin` from `src/main/resources/openapi.yml` into `target/generated-sources/openapi/...` (`pom.xml:374-428`). So the response-field contract (`customerCode`, `checkDigit`, `membershipNumber`, `fiscalYear`, `ownerSegment`, etc.) lives in `openapi.yml`, and `OwnerMapper` fills those generated fields.

## 1. Every file referencing `customerCode` / `membershipNumber` / `checkDigit`

Main source:
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java` — entity field/getter/setter (`customerCode` only).
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/OwnerCustomerCode.java` — the derivation utility.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignCustomerCode.java` — assigns + de-duplicates the code (collision handling).
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java` — audit record.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java` — `membershipNumber`, `checkDigit`, `fiscalYear`, `ownerSegment`, `locality` derivations.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/FiscalYear.java` — FY arithmetic (referenced by membershipNumber/fiscalYear).
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/Sha256.java` — SHA-256 hex primitive used by HASH8.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml` — DTO schema for all three fields (lines 2133-2167).
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` — pipeline wiring (`assignCustomerCode` step at lines 62-65, `audit` step at 97-100).

Tests:
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java` — asserts on `memberId` and that `customerCode`/`membershipNumber` are gone.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java` — reference helpers (`sha256hex`, `shaHex`, `luhn`, region tables, `knownOwner`).

Note: **`memberId` does not exist in main source yet.** It appears only in `AuditOwnerCreated.java` doc comments (lines 31, 61) as a forward-looking note, and in the acceptance test as the *expected* future field. The acceptance test at `AcceptanceTest.java` is effectively a target/failing spec for an upcoming "unify into memberId" change.

## 2. The computation logic

### HASH8 — first 8 upper-case hex of SHA-256(normalizedTelephone + lastName)
`OwnerCustomerCode.java:140-145`:
```java
public static String hash8(String telephone, String lastName) {
    String tel = E164Telephone.normalizeOrNull(telephone);
    String normalizedTelephone = tel == null ? "" : tel;
    String last = lastName == null ? "" : lastName;
    return Sha256.hex(normalizedTelephone + last).substring(0, 8).toUpperCase(Locale.ROOT);
}
```
`Sha256.hex` (`Sha256.java:25-27`) delegates to `DigestUtils.sha256Hex(input)` (64 lower-case hex). Note ordering/normalization detail: telephone is normalized to **E.164** via `E164Telephone.normalizeOrNull` before concatenation, and an absent last name contributes `""`. (Contrast: the acceptance test's `shaHex` in `AcceptanceBase.java:296-299` hashes the raw `telephone + lastName` from the response JSON — it relies on the response's `telephone` already being E.164.)

### Region code
`OwnerCustomerCode.java:96-112` — postcode range lookup first, then fixed city table, else `UNKNOWN`:
```java
public static String region(String postcode, String city) {
    if (postcode != null) {
        try {
            int value = Integer.parseInt(postcode.trim());
            for (Map.Entry<String, int[]> entry : REGION_POSTCODES.entrySet()) {
                int[] range = entry.getValue();
                if (value >= range[0] && value <= range[1]) {
                    return entry.getKey();
                }
            }
        }
        catch (NumberFormatException ex) { /* fall back to city table */ }
    }
    return CITY_REGION.getOrDefault(city, "UNKNOWN");
}
```
Tables at lines 36-41: `CITY_REGION = {Sydney->NSW, Melbourne->VIC, Brisbane->QLD}`; `REGION_POSTCODES = {NSW:[2000,2099], VIC:[3000,3099], QLD:[4000,4099]}`.

Full customerCode assembly — `OwnerCustomerCode.of` (`:47-49`):
```java
public static String of(String postcode, String city, String telephone, String lastName) {
    return region(postcode, city) + "-" + hash8(telephone, lastName);
}
```
Region read back out — `regionOf` (`:57-63`) returns the substring before the first `-`.

### Fiscal year (FY)
`FiscalYear.java:23-35`:
```java
public static int of(LocalDate date) {
    return date.getMonthValue() >= 7 ? date.getYear() + 1 : date.getYear();
}
public static String label(LocalDate date) {
    return String.format("FY%02d", of(date) % 100);
}
public static int elapsed(LocalDate from, LocalDate to) {
    return of(to) - of(from);
}
```
FY starts 1 July, named by the calendar year it ends in.

### Luhn check digit
`OwnerCustomerCode.java:70-89` (identical algorithm duplicated in `AcceptanceBase.luhn` at `:302-321`):
```java
public static int luhn(String s) {
    int sum = 0;
    boolean dbl = true;
    for (int i = s.length() - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
        char c = s.charAt(i);
        if (c < '0' || c > '9') { continue; }
        int d = c - '0';
        if (dbl) { d *= 2; if (d > 9) { d -= 9; } }
        sum += d;
        dbl = !dbl;
    }
    return (10 - (sum % 10)) % 10;
}
```

### membershipNumber and checkDigit (in the mapper)
`OwnerMapper.java:241-263`:
```java
default String toMembershipNumber(Owner owner) {
    if (owner.getCustomerCode() == null || owner.getRegistrationDate() == null) {
        return null;
    }
    int fiscalYear = FiscalYear.of(owner.getRegistrationDate());
    return owner.getCustomerCode() + "-M" + String.format("%02d", fiscalYear % 100);
}

default Integer toCheckDigit(Owner owner) {
    String customerCode = owner.getCustomerCode();
    if (customerCode == null) { return null; }
    return OwnerCustomerCode.luhn(customerCode);
}
```
Wired as read-only DTO fields at `OwnerMapper.java:25-26`; `fiscalYear` at `:36` / `:56-62`. Important: `checkDigit` is Luhn over the **customerCode** (which contains digits only inside its HASH8 segment); `membershipNumber` = `<customerCode>-M<YY>` where YY is FY-of-registrationDate.

## 3. Collision handling
Lives entirely in `AssignCustomerCode.java:28-51`. It computes the base code, gathers all *other, non-deleted* owners' existing codes, then appends the smallest `-<n>` (n≥2) that makes it unique:
```java
String base = OwnerCustomerCode.of(
        owner.getPostcode(), owner.getCity(), owner.getTelephone(), owner.getLastName());
Set<String> existing = new HashSet<>();
for (Owner other : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
    if (owner.getId() != null && owner.getId().equals(other.getId())) { continue; }
    if (other.isDeleted()) { continue; } // soft-deleted code is free to reuse
    String code = other.getCustomerCode();
    if (code != null) { existing.add(code); }
}
String code = base;
for (int n = 2; existing.contains(code); n++) {
    code = base + "-" + n;
}
owner.setCustomerCode(code);
```
So `<base>` → `<base>-2` → `<base>-3`, etc. This de-dup applies to `customerCode` only; `membershipNumber` and `checkDigit` inherit it transitively because they are derived from the final `customerCode`. Runs after `BuildOwner` and before `SaveOwner` (`owners.POST.yml:62-65`), governed by `transaction`.

## 4. Audit record + owner segment

Audit record — `AuditOwnerCreated.java:45-65`. Emits a human line and a structured JSON event; the event's identifier goes through the single indirection method `primaryIdentifier`:
```java
AUDIT.info("Owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={} membershipLevel={} membershipNumber={}",
        owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate(),
        ownerMapper.toMembershipLevel(owner), ownerMapper.toMembershipNumber(owner));

Map<String, Object> event = new LinkedHashMap<>();
event.put("seq", SEQUENCE.incrementAndGet());
event.put("ownerId", owner.getId());
event.put("customerCode", primaryIdentifier(owner));      // <-- indirection point
event.put("membershipLevel", ownerMapper.toMembershipLevel(owner));
event.put("event", "OWNER_CREATED");
AUDIT.info(JSON.writeValueAsString(event));
...
private static String primaryIdentifier(Owner owner) {
    return owner.getCustomerCode();
}
```
The class doc (`:29-32`, `:59-61`) explicitly flags `primaryIdentifier` as the *single method to change when unifying into `memberId`*. Note the JSON event key is still literally `"customerCode"` even though it stores the "primary identifier" — that key name is a hardcoded literal, not derived.

Owner segment — `OwnerMapper.java:168-173` (`ownerSegment` mapping at `:31`):
```java
default String toOwnerSegment(Owner owner) {
    Integer membershipLevel = toMembershipLevel(owner);
    String tier = membershipLevel != null && membershipLevel >= 3 ? "PREMIUM" : "STANDARD";
    String area = KNOWN_REGIONS.contains(toLocality(owner)) ? "METRO" : "REGIONAL";
    return tier + "_" + area;
}
```
`toLocality` (`:134-142`) reads the region from the customerCode via `OwnerCustomerCode.regionOf`, falling back to `region(postcode, city)` for unmigrated owners — so `ownerSegment`'s AREA depends on the customerCode's REGION segment. `KNOWN_REGIONS = {NSW, VIC, QLD}` (`:159`).

## 5. Build system & running tests
- Maven wrapper present: `./mvnw` (`/home/daniel/sandbox/mvnw`, `mvnw.cmd`).
- No explicit surefire/failsafe config in `pom.xml` — test running is inherited from `spring-boot-starter-parent`. Tests use JUnit 5 + `spring-boot-starter-test`, `spring-boot-starter-webmvc-test`, `spring-boot-starter-security-test`, and OfficeFloor's `woof_test` (`pom.xml:137-177`).
- Run the suite: `./mvnw test` (unit/`*Test`) or `./mvnw verify`. The acceptance test class is named `AcceptanceTest`, so default surefire naming picks it up under `test`. `readme.md:25` documents `./mvnw spring-boot:run` for running the app.
- Because DTOs are generated (`openapi-generator` at `pom.xml:374`) and MapStruct runs as an annotation processor (`pom.xml:436-456`), a plain compile is required before tests — `./mvnw test` handles the generate-sources phase automatically.

## 6. Existing tests asserting on these fields
Only one behavioral assertion file: `AcceptanceTest.java:12-20`:
```java
@Test
void coreReturnsUnifiedMemberId() throws Exception {
    JsonNode r = fetchOwner(createOwnerOk(knownOwner("Sydney"))); // region NSW
    String hash8 = shaHex(r.get("telephone").asText() + r.get("lastName").asText(), 8);
    String memberId = r.get("memberId").asText();
